{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0106",
  "reason": "Check disk space per KB-017 since files won't save"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, I'm sorry this has dragged on, and thanks for sticking with it. I've found the problem: your laptop's drive is almost full. Only about 9 GB of 256 GB is free (around 3.5%), and when it gets that low Windows can't save files. Here's how to free up space:\n1. Empty the Recycle Bin, then delete or move anything in your Downloads folder that you don't need.\n2. Go to Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files. Select the temporary files and old Windows Update files, then click Remove.\n3. Turn on OneDrive Files On-Demand. Right-click the OneDrive cloud icon near the clock, open Settings, and turn on 'Files On-Demand' (or 'Free up space'). Your files stay in the cloud until you open them.\n4. Go to Settings > Apps and uninstall any apps you no longer use.\nWe need to get free space above about 26 GB (10%). Once you've done these steps, please reply to this ticket. I'll check your laptop again and confirm the space has gone up. If it's still too low, I'll pass it straight to our hardware team to look at a bigger drive or a replacement laptop.",
  "internal_note": "User says this is his third request, so earlier tickets may exist. Laptop BL-LT-0106 (Win 11, online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:49 UTC) has 9.0 of 256 GB free (3.5%) and an active low-disk warning. This matches KB-017: files fail to save under 10% free. Sent the user the KB-017 cleanup steps (Recycle Bin/Downloads, temp files and old WU files, OneDrive Files On-Demand, uninstall unused apps). Waiting for the user to confirm cleanup, then re-run check_device_status. If still under 10% (about 25.6 GB) after cleanup, escalate to Tier 2 for a larger drive or replacement, per KB-017. Account is active with no lockouts. User is very frustrated, so please follow up quickly.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
